    "summary": "Model complete and checks passed.\n\nROOT CAUSE OF THE FAILURE: an instance error, not a decision error. Both Abutment 0 and Abutment 1 bearing groups had been written with \"fixed\": true for plain laminated elastomeric bearings. This contradicts the description (both abutments carry ordinary plain laminated elastomeric bearings — no fixed/sliding split is stated) and MR-03, whose applicability for family == 'laminated_elastomeric' with sliding == false gives longitudinal = \"spring\" (not fixed). The inconsistent input corrupted the topology/model check and produced the empty suspect list.\n\nREPAIR: corrected the instance (supports[0/1].bearing.fixed -> false) with write_instance; the accepted dofs (vertical spring, longitudinal spring, rotation free) then matched MR-03. Regenerated the model successfully.\n\nMODEL SUMMARY (spine_beam_2d, simply supported single 30 m span, 3 precast prestressed small-box girders of C40, girder self-weight only):\n- girder.single A = 1.13893 m^2, I = 0.354917 m^4; combined A = 3.41679 m^2, I = 1.06475 m^4 (MR-02)\n- Ec = 3.25e4 MPa, gamma = 26.0 kN/m3 (JTG D60-2015 4.2.1); w = 88.836 kN/m, m = 9.0557 t/m (MR-07)\n- Bearings: plain laminated elastomeric, 2 per girder end x 3 girders = 6 per line (MR-04), a=300 mm, b=400 mm, 5 x 8 mm layers; S = 10.714, Kv = 8.518e6 kN/m, Kh = 1.8e4 kN/m (JTG 3362-2018 8.7); dofs vertical spring / longitudinal spring / rotation free (MR-03)\n- Live load: JTG D60-2015 Class II, two-way, 2 lanes, xi = 1.0, qk = 7.875 kN/m, Pk = 240 kN (span 1)\n\nKEY RESULTS: f1 = 3.402 Hz (impact factor mu = 0.2006, JTG D60-2015 4.3.2); support reactions 1332.55 kN each summing to 2665.09 kN = gamma*A*L (L3-1/L3-2 satisfied); self-weight midspan moment 9994.1 kNm; live-load (Class II) max positive moment 6449.6 kNm."
